    "# AHR — Targeted mechanical JSON/schema/calculation repair replay\n",
    "\n**Technical reliability follow-up · targeted 8-record replay · paid calls OFF by default**\n\nThis notebook does **not** regenerate the 300 formal State-Aware Evidence v4 workflows. It replays only the frozen outputs that failed for a **mechanical structured-output reason**: duplicate JSON keys or a deterministic calculation mismatch.\n\n## Single intended intervention\n\nEach target gets **one constrained, no-tools repair request**. The repair is instructed to preserve the substantive environmental recommendation and evidence choices unless a listed mechanical error makes that impossible, while returning one complete JSON object that satisfies the unchanged State-Aware v4 schema and validator.\n\nThis is deliberately separate from the compact-correction experiment. It tests a dedicated structural/mechanical repair protocol, not evidence selection or environmental reasoning. The frozen v4 results remain unchanged.\n"
   ]
